WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.516
- Why is it so hard to be on time?

00:00:01.516 --> 00:00:04.357
Like, why does five to 10
always become 20 to 30?

00:00:04.357 --> 00:00:09.344
(jazzy piano music)

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:11.479
If my dab is on fleek, am I lit?

00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:13.153
- Why is it a problem if I like anime?

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:14.636
- Why do black people look at your shoes

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:15.543
before they greet you?

00:00:15.543 --> 00:00:18.615
- Why are we more likely to
engage in the new dance trend

00:00:18.615 --> 00:00:20.535
than we are to get involved in politics

00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:21.601
or opening a business?

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.421
- How did watermelon become our thing?

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:24.833
Like, everybody should love watermelon.

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:27.084
- Why do you get upset when I
don't like a black celebrity?

00:00:27.084 --> 00:00:29.249
- Race aside, some
people are just terrible.

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:30.519
- Why do we call each other the n-word,

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:32.865
but get vehemently upset
when a white person

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:33.655
uses the n-word?

00:00:33.655 --> 00:00:36.375
- It drains my soul to hear the word,

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:39.415
and I just don't understand
how people who have

00:00:39.415 --> 00:00:43.557
any understanding of
history can use that word.

00:00:43.557 --> 00:00:44.717
(upbeat drum and horn music)

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:45.997
- Why is my natural hair,

00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:48.301
the hair that grows out of my head,

00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:50.136
seen as a political statement?

00:00:50.136 --> 00:00:51.681
- Why do we think people
with light skin look better

00:00:51.681 --> 00:00:52.760
than people with dark skin?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.712
- Do you really believe
that black is beautiful?

00:00:54.712 --> 00:00:57.005
- Or is that just something
you say 'cause it sounds cool?

00:00:57.005 --> 00:00:58.853
- Why do some black people
say that you're pretty

00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:00.474
for a dark-skinned girl?

00:01:00.474 --> 00:01:04.005
- When that is said to me,
it still makes me feel like

00:01:04.005 --> 00:01:05.328
the ugliest little black thing.

00:01:05.328 --> 00:01:07.098
- Why do some black men
only date white women?

00:01:07.098 --> 00:01:10.288
- Why is it okay for black
men to date white women

00:01:10.288 --> 00:01:12.901
but not okay for a black woman
to date outside her race?

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.736
(rhythmic drum music)

00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:16.143
- Why do you protest black lives matter–

00:01:16.143 --> 00:01:18.116
- And then tear each other
down in the next breath?

00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:20.911
- Why do we say that we don't
want to be seen as a monolith,

00:01:20.911 --> 00:01:23.812
but then try to take
people's black cards away

00:01:23.812 --> 00:01:27.524
for not liking something
that's supposedly black?

00:01:27.524 --> 00:01:30.500
- Why are we so quick to support
a non-black-owned business

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.833
but then hesitate when it's
a black-owned business?

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.161
- I mean, is there a cutoff
time for this whole homophobia

00:01:36.161 --> 00:01:37.207
thing in the black community?

00:01:37.207 --> 00:01:38.903
'Cause I'm really looking forward to that.

00:01:38.903 --> 00:01:41.036
- Why is growing up without a
father so common in our race?

00:01:41.036 --> 00:01:43.703
- Why don't we like to confront
our mental health issues?

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:47.681
Therapy is such a wonderful
and magical place.

00:01:47.681 --> 00:01:49.441
(rhythmic clapping music)

00:01:49.441 --> 00:01:51.276
- Why is there a
checklist for being black?

00:01:51.276 --> 00:01:54.252
- Why is being educated
considered a white thing?

00:01:54.252 --> 00:01:57.505
Why can't I love school and also be black?

00:01:57.505 --> 00:02:00.844
- Why do I have to be mixed
in order to have long hair?

00:02:00.844 --> 00:02:02.999
- Why do you think well-off
black people don't know

00:02:02.999 --> 00:02:04.279
what it means to be black?

00:02:04.279 --> 00:02:06.529
- Black isn't only defined by adversity.

00:02:06.529 --> 00:02:08.058
- Why do some black people say,

00:02:08.058 --> 00:02:10.043
oh I have Native American in my family,

00:02:10.043 --> 00:02:13.339
in order to feel
interesting or more valuable

00:02:13.339 --> 00:02:14.800
than other black people around them?

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.550
- Why can't we just
acknowledge that there are

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:19.142
a bunch of different types of
black people walking around,

00:02:19.142 --> 00:02:21.659
and they're all amazing
and unique and special

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:22.630
in their own way?

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.614
- We, within the black
community, are so quick to

00:02:25.614 --> 00:02:29.318
kind of tear each other down
and to look towards other races

00:02:29.318 --> 00:02:32.247
in terms of their success and
in terms of what they have,

00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:35.120
but never want to kind of look
into the mirror ourselves?

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.214
- I love black folks,

00:02:37.214 --> 00:02:39.483
but that doesn't mean
I don't have questions.

00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:41.935
- Why are we always
looking for the discount?

00:02:41.935 --> 00:02:43.174
Shoot, I ain't gonna lie,

00:02:43.174 --> 00:02:44.411
I'll be looking at the discount, too.

00:02:44.411 --> 00:02:47.019
I don't even know why I'm saying
this, but I'm one of them.

